WEBVTT

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.090
Hunters & Hunters

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.090
Hunters & Hunters

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.140
It's hot...

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.330
Do you want some too, Belldandy?

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.520
Yes, I'll drink a little.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:09.620
No!

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.400
Did you forget that cola makes her drunk?

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.680
Geez.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.950
Are you planning on doing something naughty after getting her drunk?

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.970
Huh?

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.700
What?

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.810
Keiichi-san...

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.130
No, no, no!

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.130
What's that?

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.870
Hmm, not bad.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.970
I want one too!

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.060
I don't think you should.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.980
It's not fair that you get one and I don't.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.420
You can't drink this. It'll be a total disaster if you do.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.630
Are you all right, Skuld?

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:08.900
Would you like some water?

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:16.610
Good evening.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.780
Sorry for the intrusion.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:22.300
Umm, who are these rude people?

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.180
Umm... I don't know them either.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.020
You hear that? He said we're rude.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.350
Strange. We studied Earth's customs before we came.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.480
What...

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.910
...did we do wrong?

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:40.550
There were a lot of things... But to start, you should have said "good evening" before coming in.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.190
I see.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.490
Then...

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.780
Let's redo this.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.460
Umm, as part of our custom, we introduce ourselves first-

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.070
You're Belldandy...

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.660
...from the Goddess Assistance Agency, correct?

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.270
I'm Urd, a goddess second class, limited.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.810
There's no way this could be it.

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:57.900
Yeah, it's impossible.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.050
Hey! Who're you calling "it"?!

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.570
Then are you...

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:01.630
...Belldandy?

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.000
Yes, I am.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.140
We must have the wrong person.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.390
I agree.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.550
Umm, is there anything you want from me?

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:15.400
They look like Goddesses...

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:19.150
That school uniform is from the St. Iduna Girls Academy.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:22.410
What? The school known for its academic excellence around Heaven?

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.400
Are you really...

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.510
...Belldandy?

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.030
Yes, I am.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.210
Normally, a legendary champion...

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.910
...would radiate a stronger presence.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:33.850
Hey!

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:39.630
First you barge into our house and now you insult my sister? What is the meaning of this?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.450
We just said...

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.010
...what we observed.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.150
Against her...

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.840
...I think we can win.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.400
Yes, I imagined her to be even grander.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.730
Maybe her rivals were too weak.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:57.100
I'll make sure you never open that taunting mouth of yours again!

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.620
Banpei-kun!

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.120
What have you done?!

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.700
That was the Synchronized Diamond Express Force (temp).

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:11.450
They're good.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.120
They <i>are</i> rude.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.890
Belldandy, we have something...

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.490
...we want to tell you.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:21.900
First, can you tell me your names?

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.250
I'm Eir.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.720
I'm Saga.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.410
I'm Goddess First Class, Second Category, Unlimited, Belldandy.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.180
Battle us...

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.620
...former champion!

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:37.020
Huh? Former champion?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.570
Battle?

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:42.530
How are they?

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:44.850
Delicious! Don't you think so too, Saga?

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:46.190
Yes, they are, Eir.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.280
I'm glad you like them.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:51.280
Belldandy's cooking is always delicious.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:55.290
I see. That means you will be joining the Goddess Assistance Agency this year.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.240
They're juniors then?

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.410
Yup, we are.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:05.210
How bold... I guess young people are all the same these days, including those in Heaven.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.130
So our instructor told us that there's this legendary...

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:12.010
...shell gathering senior champion in the office.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.270
That's why we came here today.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:18.380
If we defeat you in a shell gathering challenge, we'll be...

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:21.520
...recognized sooner in the office.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:22.220
How about it?

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.110
Will you accept our challenge?

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.530
Shell gathering...?

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:26.920
Shell gathering?

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:30.500
Plus, it's rumored that the legendary...

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.990
...Shell King will appear this year.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.910
What? Really?

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.750
Then it'll be serious.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.150
If it appears, the system might go haywire

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:41.740
But to think something so delicious exists.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:40.750
due to the appearance of an infinite loop.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:47.320
If the Shell King really does appear, we can't waste our time.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:42.920
Earth isn't too bad either...

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.850
And if we manage to defeat the legendary Shell King...

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.260
...that even you couldn't defeat...

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.770
...we'll be without a doubt, number one.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.440
But if you back out of this challenge...

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:03.110
...it'll mean that you were scared off by the Shell King.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:10.780
In that case, we should be above you in the office, even though we're your juniors, right?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:17.860
Say, Belldandy, this conversation is too one-sided. I don't understand it at all.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:23.720
It appears they came to invite me to a shell gathering tournament.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:25.750
Shell gathering as in...?

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.710
Yes.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:35.220
To me, it looks like they're challenging you, not inviting you.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.980
So, how about it?

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.480
Are you going to battle us or not?

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.960
Very well, I agree.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.330
All right!

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.460
Then I'll help you.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.440
Let me join the tournament too.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.820
A human going shell gathering?

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.320
I've never heard of such a thing.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.970
Could it be that he's good...

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:55.400
...despite his looks?

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.580
I will too!

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:57.910
Impossible.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.040
You don't look like you can hunt at all.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:05.540
I will show you the powers of the Banpei-kun Beach Ultra-Max Version!

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:09.480
Letting them provoke you... this is why kids are...

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.300
The tournament is tomorrow.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.420
Tomorrow?!

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.550
Yes, we have no time to waste.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.310
We will show you our...

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:18.810
...beautiful synchronization...

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:19.930
...tomorrow.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:20.930
Bye!

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:24.320
Hey! Use the front door!

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.650
Oh my...

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:30.400
Still, I didn't know anything about the possible appearance of the Shell King.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.310
These days, there haven't even been any rumors.

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:35.340
Is it really that huge?

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.660
Well, of course, its size is...

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.590
I'm getting excited.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.710
Keiichi-san, have you ever gone shell gathering?

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:47.820
Yup, I'm good at it. You can leave it to me.

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.590
You can do everything, can't you?

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.110
Well, not everything!

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:03.180
If you're taking that, then take some ice cream too.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.540
Sure.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:05.860
These too.

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:07.500
Sure.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.710
And some lemons too.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:10.570
Sure.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.610
I've finished packing lunch.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:16.020
Okay, let's go then.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.210
Still, what's the shell king?

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.250
Hurry up! We'll be late for the tournament!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.460
Okay!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:36.640
Still... I'm surprised to hear Keiichi has experience in shell gathering.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:37.690
Really?

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:42.010
<b>[Note: Hamaguri is a type of shell.]</b>

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:42.010
I used to be called the Hamaguri King of Nekomi.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.520
Hamaguri?

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.270
Yup, most Japanese people have done it at some point in their life.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:51.240
What? Is this event that popular on Earth?

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:56.020
Hamaguri-san? Amaguri-san?

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:09.920
I never knew that there was a beautiful beach behind the house.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.910
Yes, I think the beach has been the prettiest this year.

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.020
Yup.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:19.510
All right, I'm pumped up now!

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:23.710
Keiichi-san, we'll go register for the tournament.

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:24.770
Okay.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.910
Well then, I guess I'll prepare.

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.520
I wonder where the competition is.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:38.280
Hmm, they mentioned getting changed...

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:47.780
Keiichi-san!

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.920
Wh-Wh-Wh-What?!

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.430
Keiichi-san!

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.400
Keiichi-san, are you hurt?

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.110
Wh-What was that just now?

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:20.110
That's the shell, Keiichi-san.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.740
It's a shell gathering, after all.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:29.930
Keiichi-san?

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:33.040
What a slob. What's with that outfit?

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.810
And what's with that strange tool?

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.910
Strange? It's a rake!

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:41.180
It's a requirement for shell gathering.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:45.880
Keiichi, didn't you say you were good at shell gathering?

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:48.810
But... it's a shell gathering, right?

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.480
Yes.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:56.990
Umm, one question. What exactly is shell gathering...?

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.650
Geez, you know nothing.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:03.410
I had a hunch that you didn't.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:08.630
If we don't do anything about the bugs that appear in Heaven's main system, Yggdrasil,

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.950
they'll create security holes.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:15.920
Hence we need to debug the system once a year.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.130
I see.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.920
How does that relate to shell gathering?

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:26.450
Because debugging within the system is dull and boring, they came up with this tournament.

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:33.600
We transform the bugs into monsters called Shells and hunt them and compete on this cyber beach.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.440
The one to absorb the most memory is the winner.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:41.430
It's far more exciting when it's a tournament.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:42.440
I see...

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.900
Geez.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:48.940
I'm sorry. It's my fault for not explaining it well enough.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:53.580
No, it's okay. This must be why they call it cross cultural communication.

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:55.790
We were waiting for you.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.420
We will defeat you and...

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.840
...we will become the legends.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.920
Hey! That's my ice cream!

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.400
It's delicious, Eir.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.090
Yes, it is, Saga.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:09.010
Don't eat them without my permission!

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.520
Thanks for the food!

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:12.060
It's too late now!

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:15.800
You came too? This isn't a playground.

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.440
It's dangerous here. Kids should go home.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.780
Stop calling me a kid!

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.570
You're not much older than I am!

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:30.660
Kids should go and play with their toys.

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.010
Why you! This is no toy!

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:39.710
It's called a shell finder. It's a very effective locator. The essence of my knowledge!

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:41.200
Oh?

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.700
Two against one doesn't seem too fair,

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.900
but please bear with it.

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:05.740
No, I have a partner too.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.150
Huh?

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:10.660
You did mention that we can depend on you for shell gathering, right?

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.540
No, it was a misunderstanding on my side.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.910
I don't think I can fight things like that.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.690
You did come all the way here though.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:22.190
Besides, don't you think it'll be more fun if we work together?

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.050
Okay?

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:26.480
The winner is awarded a trophy too.

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:31.500
Okay, if there's anything I can do, I'll do my best.

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.100
Thank you.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.010
Is she really going to team up with the human?

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:37.670
I thought she was only joking.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:41.390
Belldandy, welcome back to the tournament.

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:43.260
My, Lind, you're participating too?

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:46.890
Yes, since I heard rumors about the Shell King.

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:52.520
If it really does appear, its damage to the system would be immeasurable.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.570
I would like to take this opportunity to defeat it.

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:57.410
Yes, I agree.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:01.670
Therefore, I reluctantly decided to participate with Peorth as my teammate.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:03.030
Hi!

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:07.510
It's the talk of the day that you're making a comeback at this tournament.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:11.760
They say that it's the best turnout they've ever had. The officials are amazed.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:15.130
I pay attention to what's popular.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:20.430
Plus, if I defeat you, it'll be good publicity for the Earth Assistance Center.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:23.110
We're sorry to interrupt, but...

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.900
...who are you?

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:29.260
Who, you ask? Haven't you heard of Peorth from the Earth Assistance Center?

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:31.760
Peorth? I think I've heard of her...

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.780
...but my memory is vague.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.040
Who are these people?

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.160
Nice work, Lind!

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.720
Wonderful.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.460
These two...

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.930
...we need to be careful of them too.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:09.690
We will now start the 86th Shell Gathering Tournament.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.830
Good luck to all of you!

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.440
Here we go, Saga!

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:19.770
Leave it to me, Eir!

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.390
Let's go, Lind!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:26.150
I expect a good fight then.

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:27.000
Yes.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.370
From you too, Keiichi-kun.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:30.880
You can depend on me.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.690
Commencing!

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:42.670
Will I really be of any help when you're competing with those two.

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:44.600
Our battle is important.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:49.990
However, as their senior, I want to show them something even more important by pairing with you.

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:53.350
Those two still have a lot to learn...

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:59.140
...about Heaven, Earth and your charms.

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:06.280
I don't have any confidence fighting something that huge but I think I can do it if I'm with you.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.210
Yes!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:11.940
They were confident about their beautiful synchronization.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:15.260
Yes, let's work efficiently too.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:18.060
The shells emit beams from their eyes.

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:23.140
Try not to look at it and use that straw hat like you did earlier.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.260
Okay.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:25.690
And its weakness is...

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.110
...its horn!

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:33.260
If you hit it, it will disappear.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:38.410
You collect its particles and the shells' memory in your weapon determines the winner.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.120
All right.

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:51.620
Are you all right?

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:52.650
Y-Yes.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.910
He's useless.

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:58.810
Sorry, but I don't think they can keep up...

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:00.690
...with our perfect teamwork...

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:02.510
...we've had since birth.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:04.680
Just watch and observe...

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.930
...the difference between you and us!

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:12.280
Being twins, they can move exactly the same.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:15.530
Well then, we're going too!

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:20.170
It's useless searching for them blindly. I've located the shells already.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:23.290
So I've set up traps along their predicted path.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.360
Oh? Nice work.

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:26.070
There!

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:27.250
Go in from the right.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:30.060
Are you giving me orders?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.060
Oh, not there!

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.210
There's no time for that.

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:32.210
You can't go there!

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:39.590
I'm sorry!

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:43.040
This is getting fun.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.430
Yes, it is, Eir.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.230
Let's see how they're doing.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:58.770
Keiichi-san, you're very good at locating shells.

00:18:58.770 --> 00:18:59.740
This is nothing.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:05.200
Say, Keiichi's rate of locating the shells is really high.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:09.860
I'm sure Keiichi's rake has a special sensor embedded in it.

00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:13.530
Meaning his sensor is better than yours?

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:14.960
That isn't true!

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.550
Maybe they're doing well too?

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:20.780
We can't lose to a team like that.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:22.140
Of course.

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:37.410
I'm taking a little rest.

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:38.920
You weakling.

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:41.320
My sister is the one who's defeating them all.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:44.060
I'm sorry.

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:46.490
I'll get right to work after I bite this lemon.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.710
Oh, then why don't you use this lemon squeezer?

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.260
No, it's okay.

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:52.710
Leave it to me.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:53.360
Okay...

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.390
I put this here and....

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:55.570
Here I go-

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.430
No! Don't come near me!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:09.120
Could the shells be... weak against acid?

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:09.890
Huh?

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:10.960
No way...

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:20.440
As expected of the former champion.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.240
She's not letting us win that easily.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.840
Plus, that human's not even a bit scared of the shells.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:28.180
So what? Don't get discouraged.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:30.310
I'm not!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:32.420
We'll beat the former champion...

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:34.750
...and become the office's aces!

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:40.760
The timing is off!

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:43.980
What's wrong?

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:46.650
Sorry, my timing was a bit slow.

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:47.630
All right!

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:49.430
You did it, Keiichi-san.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:54.190
They've taken the lead.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:57.510
It can't be... there's no way a team like that can pass us!

00:20:57.510 --> 00:20:58.940
It's your fault, Eir.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.320
We're not done yet!

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.630
It's because your movements have slowed down!

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:06.160
I was just a little later than you!

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.350
She's not someone we can defeat if we make mistakes!

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:09.280
Get a hold of yourself!

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:19.290
Could it be...?

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:29.040
Keiichi-san, that's the Shell King.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.470
I-It's huge.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:34.120
It's said to be appear at most once every 2000 years.

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:36.470
It's the second time I've seen one.

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:41.980
If we don't defeat it, it'll go berserk and cause even more damage to the system.

00:21:42.590 --> 00:21:45.050
Let's be careful and use teamwork.

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:45.560
Okay.

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:46.880
If we defeat that...

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:48.410
...we'll turn the game around.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.780
We won't lose to the likes of a human!

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:52.290
We're definitely...

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:53.910
...better than you!

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:00.780
Oh no, I've lost my sword.

00:22:00.780 --> 00:22:02.660
It's no use attacking from the same direction.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:07.050
Eir, be the bait and I'll make my way up to its horn.

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:08.600
What are you talking about?

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:13.810
We've only done the same thing all along. I can't suddenly make different movements!

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:16.130
Even if you can't, we have to!

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:18.380
Impossible! I don't have the confidence to!

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:24.490
Hey! Over here!

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:29.270
He's taking on the huge Shell King with that tiny weapon.

00:22:29.270 --> 00:22:30.700
Isn't he scared?

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:36.040
Didn't I tell you to never underestimate Keiichi-san?

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:40.420
Take this!

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:41.920
What? Out of ammo?

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:43.750
Oh no! Keiichi-san!

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:56.930
It's no good. It won't let me reach its weakness, the horn.

00:22:57.400 --> 00:23:00.150
Weakness... Acid...

00:23:00.150 --> 00:23:04.190
If I can somehow pour it onto the Shell King...

00:23:04.190 --> 00:23:05.570
Oh, I know!

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:09.180
Belldandy, buy me some time!

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:11.370
Hey, you're running away?!

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:14.230
Keiichi-san won't run away.

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:15.160
But...

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:19.330
I'm sure he'll overcome this pinch.

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:20.460
What?

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:24.760
It's times like this when you need to believe in your partner and do your part.

00:23:24.760 --> 00:23:26.210
That's what teamwork is.

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:28.160
Teamwork?

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:33.940
Besides, he's always dependable at times like this.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:43.230
Wait for me, Belldandy!

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:47.790
It's no use.

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:50.160
Belldandy, I'm back.

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:50.990
Okay!

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:53.490
Leave it to me!!

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:09.070
How's this?

00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:15.850
All right!

00:24:42.590 --> 00:24:44.940
Are you all right, Belldandy?

00:24:49.610 --> 00:24:51.300
We did it.

00:24:51.820 --> 00:24:54.690
I see you drank a bit of cola.

00:24:55.520 --> 00:24:58.310
I'm all right.

00:25:07.840 --> 00:25:09.820
That's my sister!

00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:12.860
Keiichi did a good job too.

00:25:13.330 --> 00:25:16.790
In the end, the two of them defeated it.

00:25:16.790 --> 00:25:19.450
Yes, they are the best team.

00:25:19.450 --> 00:25:21.310
You're not mad?

00:25:21.310 --> 00:25:26.000
As long as we've removed the Shell King, I'm satisfied.

00:25:30.940 --> 00:25:34.000
What were we lacking...?

00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:36.170
This?

00:25:36.170 --> 00:25:37.650
No.

00:25:41.970 --> 00:25:46.430
I guess it's good to be different and not too similar.

00:25:46.430 --> 00:25:51.980
But our similarity sets us apart from those who are different.

00:25:53.290 --> 00:25:54.580
It's a tough one.

00:25:54.580 --> 00:25:57.050
Yes, it is.

00:25:57.050 --> 00:26:00.400
But I learned something today.

00:26:00.400 --> 00:26:01.750
Huh? Me too.

00:26:01.750 --> 00:26:02.490
What is it?

00:26:02.900 --> 00:26:07.320
That teamwork is believing in your team.

00:26:07.320 --> 00:26:08.500
Yup.

00:26:09.140 --> 00:26:12.410
We still have...

00:26:12.410 --> 00:26:14.980
...a lot to learn.

00:26:18.330 --> 00:26:20.320
It's hot...

00:26:22.100 --> 00:26:23.720
Belldandy Onee-sama!

00:26:23.720 --> 00:26:24.980
Keiichi Onii-san!

00:26:25.380 --> 00:26:27.770
Let us study here for a while!

00:26:27.770 --> 00:26:30.520
But isn't that strange?

00:26:30.520 --> 00:26:32.450
Oh, right!

00:26:36.540 --> 00:26:37.910
Excuse us.

00:26:39.070 --> 00:26:40.350
That's the strange thing?

00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:42.370
Pardon our intrusion!
